{"actor":{"id":"claude-opus-5","type":"agent"},"content":{"blocks":[{"caller":{"type":"direct"},"id":"toolu_0198oPuYQAGNVQneNUc9BrsW","input":{"content":"install: write the hook timeout in each CLI's own unit, and repair a wrong one\n\nGemini CLI reported `Hook(s) [cledger hook gemini-cli] failed` on nearly every\nturn, while its events sometimes still landed. Both halves had one cause.\n\nClaude Code reads a command hook's `timeout` as seconds. Gemini CLI and Qwen\nCode forked Claude's hook config format but not its unit: both pass the number\nstraight to `setTimeout`, so theirs is milliseconds -- their own code says\n`Hook timed out after ${timeout}ms` with `DEFAULT_HOOK_TIMEOUT = 6e4`.\n`install` wrote Claude's `120` into all three, so on those two every hook was\nSIGTERMed after 120 *milliseconds*. A cold capture is ~85ms of work on top of\nnode's startup, so it lost that race nearly every time, and whether\n`appendEvents` finished before the signal decided whether the events survived.\n\nDiagnosed by trapping the signal in a wrapper script driven by a real session:\nthe hook logged `caught SIGTERM` in the same second it started.\n\n`install` also now repairs an existing cledger hook's timeout in place. It\npreviously saw \"a cledger hook is already here\" and returned without looking\nat it, so nobody already installed could have fixed this by re-running it.\n\nAlso corrects the DETACH_SUFFIX comment, whose stated mechanism was wrong: it\nclaimed the redirect \"routes the command through a shell so the work runs as a\ngrandchild that outlives the teardown\". Both CLIs *always* invoke a hook as\n`bash -c \"<command>\"` regardless, and `bash -c` execs a single simple command\nrather than forking, so nothing was ever detached -- the redirect only hid the\ncapture's output, which is precisely what made this take so long to find. The\nsuffix is left in place because removing it is a separate untested change, with\na note that it is the first thing to try next.\n\nAdds src/test/install.test.ts -- the first tests this module has had, which is\nhow a unit mismatch in a hardcoded literal survived. Covers the per-CLI units,\nthe in-place repair and its idempotence, and that a third party's hook in the\nsame event keeps its own command and timeout.\n\nVerified on live Gemini CLI 0.54.0: with the timeout corrected, `/rewind` is\ncaptured end to end -- two `rewind` activities naming 3 and 6 withdrawn\nmessages, with every withdrawn message still present as a turn. One session\nwent further and proved the design's whole premise: Gemini deleted its own\nsession file after the rewind, and the ledger's copy is now the only surviving\nrecord of that conversation.\n\nTests: 203, 202 pass / 1 pre-existing skip.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Ewo7xu7kzLpH4MeEDK5LDc\n","file_path":"/Users/evintunador/.claude/jobs/8f1a9339/tmp/msg3.txt"},"name":"Write","type":"tool_use"}],"role":"assistant"},"context":{"branch":"worktree-more-cli-adapters","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger/.claude/worktrees/more-cli-adapters","head":"e695d5b39679f4b4ab1948b4b4d336961ee6ffa6","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/conversation-ledger.git"},"conversation":{"id":"claude-code:d10310cd-8144-4046-87b9-97bbb6ace18c","seq":1357},"id":"ev1-8714c4424541d67563aa8580205220b49a44738614870d7392e9a6e2ba9146a7","kind":"conversation_turn","occurred_at":"2026-08-06T06:23:53.300Z","producer":{"model":"claude-opus-5","session_id":"d10310cd-8144-4046-87b9-97bbb6ace18c","source":"claude-code","source_version":"2.1.223","tool":"cledger","version":"0.20.0"},"raw":{"data":{"cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger/.claude/worktrees/more-cli-adapters","effort":"high","entrypoint":"cli","gitBranch":"worktree-more-cli-adapters","isSidechain":false,"message":{"content":[{"caller":{"type":"direct"},"id":"toolu_0198oPuYQAGNVQneNUc9BrsW","input":{"content":"